          "explanation": "Sol. Step 1: Understand the sentences • (A) introduces glucose → what it is. • (E) explains how glucose is regulated → by insulin. • (C) stresses why this regulation is important. • (B) shows what happens if levels drop too low. • (D) contrasts with what happens if levels rise too high. 44 Step 2: Build the logical flow 1. Start with A → introduces glucose. 2. Follow with E → regulation mechanism (insulin). 3. Then C → importance of regulation. 4. Then B → effect of low sugar. 5. Finally D → effect of high sugar (contrast). So the correct sequence is AECBD. Step 3: Match with options (d) AECBD Final Answer: (d) AECBD",
